/-! ### Non-vacuity on the cubic `E`

`E` is an elliptic curve with the group object `cubicGrpObj`. Batch 60 gives
`BettiDeRhamIso E` (`spec_bettiDeRhamIso_abelian`), S13 gives `TorusCohomology (cupProductOf E)`
(`torusCohomology_cupProductOf`), and the first harvest gives
`CycleClassMultiplicative (cupProductOf E)` (`harvest_cycleClassMultiplicative_curve`). So the
restated milestones apply to a real `X`, and on `E` each asks only for its genuinely open inputs.
-/

/-- On `E`, the restated exterior-power milestone asks only for `HodgeDecomposition E` and
`CupFiltered E (cupProductOf E)`. -/
example (hD : HodgeDecomposition E) (hC : CupFiltered E (cupProductOf E)) :
    letI := (torusCohomology_cupProductOf E).finite
    AbelianVarietyCohomology.IsExteriorOfWeightOne
      (abelianVarietyCohomologyOf (finbetti_finiteBetti E) (spec_bettiDeRhamIso_abelian E) hD
        (torusCohomology_cupProductOf E)) :=
  harvestBetti_isExteriorOfWeightOne_of_cupFiltered _ hD _ hC

/-- On `E`, the restated `g = 1` milestone asks only for `HodgeDecomposition E`,
`CycleClassIsHodge E` and `LefschetzOneOneHyp`. Its conclusion is also
`harvest_hodgeConjectureInDimensionLE_one E E_dim.le`, unconditionally; the point here is that
the restated hypotheses are those of a real abelian curve, not that the conclusion is new. -/
example (hD : HodgeDecomposition E) (hH : CycleClassIsHodge E) (h11 : LefschetzOneOneHyp) :
    ∀ p : ℕ, Hdg^p(E; ℚ) ≤ algebraicCycleClassSpan E p :=
  harvestBetti_hdg_le_span_abelian_g1 (spec_bettiDeRhamIso_abelian E) hD
    (torusCohomology_cupProductOf E) hH h11
    E_dim

